# The scripts that KaTTY gives the shells of its terminals keep Unix line endings on every system: a checkout on Windows converts text to CRLF by
# default, and the bash, zsh and fish of MSYS2, Git for Windows and Cygwin read a carriage return as part of each line.
*.bash text eol=lf
*.zsh text eol=lf
*.fish text eol=lf
.zshenv text eol=lf
